"prose": [
{
"from": 201,
"to": 204,
"text": "The gates run the driver's unit test of the conversion and the two new integration targets in both layout modes. `text_extent` and `stand_actions` show that the reader precedent and the run path's resolver are unmoved. Then come the pre-push gate, `stand-repeat`, which the new `stand_` target joins, and the coverage leg, where escher-driver's 97 % floor reads `Session::layout` (arch · decision/per-crate-coverage-floors)."
},
{
"from": 206,
"to": 207,
"text": "No boot-path touchpoint: no binary, role or seven_guis source changes, so there is no `role = 'smoke'` entry. The stand boots in process in every stand check. No live leg: nothing outside the tree is driven."
},
{
"from": 209,
"to": 215,
"text": "Each new check is controlled red-before-green (keeps tests S4: decision/mutation-controlled-tests). After the steps are green, /implement runs three one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries: - Rule 4 of step 1's `SizeCause` arm made unreachable in `layout_reason.rs`: the size table's case in `layout_reason`   reads failed. - `at` taken from `final_layout()` in place of the unrounded geometry: stand_layout's offset-equality case reads failed   on a sub-pixel box, or the control reads that no stand box is sub-pixel, recorded as such. - `Session::layout` given a `pump` before its read: stand_layout's no-change case reads failed."
},
{
"from": 217,
"to": 218,
"text": "Each control names the edit's text and the case by its test name, as `gate.py control` takes them (gate-contract.md §Control)."
},
{
"from": 220,
"to": 223,
"text": "The diff holds no OS-conditional site. The plan still carries the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries: the workspace test leg builds blitz-dom with `writing-mode` and `tracing` on, where the per-package runs above leave them off (test-plan · decision/per-package-green-not-workspace-green), and the cross-OS legs build the new targets on windows and macOS."
}
